WEBVTT

00:10.490 --> 00:11.820
That's right.

00:11.820 --> 00:15.500
My daily training helps me lift even the heaviest loads.

00:16.160 --> 00:19.290
That means old ladies won't have a hard time anymore.

00:19.290 --> 00:23.130
You bet. I'll carry their stuff,
and maybe even them while I'm at it!

00:24.800 --> 00:26.260
Wow.

00:26.260 --> 00:30.800
And that's how the CDF is working
wholeheartedly for the peace of this island!

00:34.010 --> 00:38.060
Wolfderful! Today's master was a hero from the CDF!

00:38.060 --> 00:41.980
They may <i>seem</i> strong, but if they didn't have a major power's protection

00:41.980 --> 00:43.610
they'd be as easy as a bug to squash.

00:43.610 --> 00:48.780
This puny island couldn't stay independent if we didn't tie into the big guy's best interests.

00:48.780 --> 00:50.860
You're watching Working Adults, with Mecha-lick and—

00:50.860 --> 00:55.030
...the intellectual young star that can handle everything from educational shows to news, Vli—

00:54.160 --> 00:55.870
Cut! Cut!

00:56.490 --> 00:58.620
You know what!? Get back in the damned costume!

01:01.960 --> 01:03.960
I can't wait for next week's episode.

02:45.060 --> 02:46.770
Okay. L1, rock!

02:47.440 --> 02:48.820
R-Right!

02:49.400 --> 02:50.900
R1, paper!

02:51.280 --> 02:52.900
Okay!

02:53.490 --> 02:55.030
Make L2 scissors.

02:55.700 --> 02:57.780
O-Okay!

02:59.030 --> 03:00.540
R3, paper!

03:00.540 --> 03:01.660
Okay!

03:03.790 --> 03:06.920
Raise L2, and make R3 rock!

03:06.920 --> 03:08.500
O-Okay!

03:10.500 --> 03:13.420
Raise R1, and make L2 scissors!

03:13.420 --> 03:17.180
Raise L1, and don't lower L3!

03:18.550 --> 03:22.470
Th-This is hard.

03:23.100 --> 03:25.770
If you can't even handle it
I might as well reject it.

03:26.100 --> 03:30.860
Who the heck's gonna use a Hekatoncheir design like this, anyway?

03:32.940 --> 03:34.860
Raise thy fifth leg!

03:37.860 --> 03:39.700
Ack!

03:39.700 --> 03:42.120
Nene, it's time to get going.

03:43.040 --> 03:44.290
Maintenance?

03:44.290 --> 03:45.080
Yes.

03:48.960 --> 03:50.590
How do I look, Grandma?

03:50.590 --> 03:53.800
Dr. Toto won't be able to resist! Just you watch!

03:53.800 --> 03:57.130
Wow, Boss! That dress just flutters!

03:57.130 --> 04:00.300
Yeah! It's love that makes a lady lovely herself!

04:01.140 --> 04:02.930
Grandma!

04:15.230 --> 04:15.860
Hey.

04:15.860 --> 04:17.700
What's going on?

04:18.320 --> 04:21.820
You guys, what's all this commotion first thing in the morning?

04:21.820 --> 04:23.450
Oh, Granny.

04:23.870 --> 04:26.700
These guys from CDF say they need to talk to us.

04:28.210 --> 04:32.130
Oho, there some kind of trouble? Just leave it to me!

04:32.130 --> 04:35.630
No, wait, I was just about to go somewhere.

04:35.630 --> 04:38.840
Grandma, I can go to the hospital by myself.

04:38.840 --> 04:39.800
But...

04:39.800 --> 04:43.800
I'll be okay! I won't get lost,
and I won't talk to strangers!

04:43.800 --> 04:46.310
If anything happens, you call me!

04:46.310 --> 04:47.600
Roger!

04:59.280 --> 05:01.610
All right, change into this.

05:02.030 --> 05:04.080
Put your clothes in there.

05:04.080 --> 05:04.870
Yes, ma'am.

05:07.450 --> 05:09.750
Away we sail, upon the unknown ocean!

05:09.750 --> 05:13.170
We make for the sea of a maiden's sweet fragrance!

05:13.170 --> 05:14.750
Sniff, sniff!

05:15.040 --> 05:16.750
Oh, a doll?

05:19.220 --> 05:22.010
Lo, thou art a ministering angel!

05:22.010 --> 05:24.470
Sei molto bella!

05:24.470 --> 05:27.770
My, aren't you talented.
Are you one of those petroid things?

05:27.770 --> 05:30.180
They're pretty well made these days, aren't they?

05:30.180 --> 05:33.190
I am no pet! I be BUER, the demon king!

05:33.190 --> 05:36.020
Shall we spend the night engaged in talks of everlasting love?

05:36.020 --> 05:39.400
Yes, yes. Ready to go then, Nene?

05:39.400 --> 05:40.650
Yes, ma'am.

05:41.570 --> 05:46.410
The <i>passionate</i> adult maintenance thou hath needs make thee giddy—

06:04.720 --> 06:06.510
Let's go, then.

06:06.510 --> 06:07.470
Of course.

06:14.400 --> 06:22.320
Cramped! Dark! Cramped! Dark! Cramped! Dark! Cramped! Dark! Cramped! Dark! Cramped! Dark!

06:24.160 --> 06:27.740
The stress and strain on your frame is within acceptable limits,

06:27.740 --> 06:30.240
and I've just finished rebalancing your bio-support system.

06:30.240 --> 06:31.790
Do you feel uncomfortable anywhere?

06:31.790 --> 06:33.500
No, Doctor. Nothing.

06:33.500 --> 06:36.960
Your senses don't feel out of tune with your body or anything?

06:36.960 --> 06:39.210
Not at all. I've been fine since I arrived.

06:39.210 --> 06:42.630
You've been in good shape since you arrived at Takumi's.

06:43.720 --> 06:45.220
It seems, indeed.

06:52.560 --> 06:54.230
You can't come in, Lean.

06:54.850 --> 06:56.850
Animals aren't allowed in the hospital.

06:56.850 --> 06:59.070
I'll be done soon, so you wait out here.

07:00.980 --> 07:06.490
Listen. Don't, and I mean <i>don't</i>,
go anywhere, you hear?

07:22.210 --> 07:24.670
This is an announcement for all island residents.

07:24.670 --> 07:28.640
A large-scale network outage has occurred.

07:28.640 --> 07:31.100
Hello? Hello!?

07:37.440 --> 07:39.520
What's this, another outage?

07:39.520 --> 07:42.440
Oh my, another one? How inconvenient.

07:42.440 --> 07:45.440
Don't worry. It's no big deal.

07:45.440 --> 07:48.240
3, 2, 1.

07:52.200 --> 07:53.040
See?

07:53.040 --> 07:57.710
The building switches over to the wired lines when this happens.

07:57.710 --> 08:01.920
Excuse me, but is it okay to continue the exam during the network outage?

08:02.550 --> 08:04.760
Of course it's okay.

08:04.760 --> 08:08.930
This hospital's owner had the idea to install countermeasures in case of catastrophic disaster.

08:09.510 --> 08:12.260
Naturally, the building has plenty of emergency power.

08:12.260 --> 08:15.640
In addition, all the wired connections

08:15.640 --> 08:18.310
have a multi-layered web of barriers to guard them.

08:18.640 --> 08:22.020
What's more, the hospital's internal infrastructure is primarily wired,

08:22.020 --> 08:25.320
so isolation from the outside won't affect treatments.

08:25.320 --> 08:28.820
Wow! The owner is incredible!

08:29.820 --> 08:31.820
That's right!

08:32.620 --> 08:34.830
Okay, clench with all your strength.

08:36.750 --> 08:38.290
Okay, good.

08:39.750 --> 08:41.920
What are you examining now?

08:41.920 --> 08:45.550
We're calibrating your strength so you can exert the exact amount you intended to,

08:45.550 --> 08:49.590
using averages of girls your age for reference.

08:49.590 --> 08:53.010
You should be able to adjust your output better now.

08:53.010 --> 08:55.770
Does that mean I can make myself super strong?

08:55.770 --> 08:58.890
We're calibrating it so that you <i>can't</i>.

08:58.890 --> 09:01.600
That level of strength would be meaningless and dangerous.

09:01.600 --> 09:05.230
And on the other hand,
thoughtlessly applying limiters is no better.

09:06.480 --> 09:08.150
The brains of living things

09:08.150 --> 09:12.110
love to issue behavioral commands that
disregard the body's structural strength,

09:12.110 --> 09:14.660
and then reflexively send precise commands afterwards.

09:14.660 --> 09:17.660
So if you released too much torque every time it happened

09:17.660 --> 09:19.250
your actions would become unpredictable,

09:17.750 --> 09:19.250
He means ordinary is best.

09:19.580 --> 09:21.620
and worsen your energy efficiency.

09:19.830 --> 09:22.250
You don't want to be called "gorilla girl," do you?

09:21.620 --> 09:24.500
Many motors operate simultaneously in a prosthetic body,

09:22.540 --> 09:24.500
Gorillas are cute.

09:24.790 --> 09:27.590
so even a small energy loss is no laughing matter.

09:24.840 --> 09:27.170
Not that I've ever seen a real one.

09:27.590 --> 09:28.630
Nonetheless, it...

09:32.380 --> 09:34.850
Your registration is complete.

09:34.850 --> 09:36.720
Please wait in the lobby.

09:39.980 --> 09:41.310
Lean!?

09:46.690 --> 09:48.650
Lean, I told you not to come in.

09:50.490 --> 09:52.030
N-No, Lean!

09:52.490 --> 09:55.070
Be quiet! They'll find you!

09:58.870 --> 10:00.250
Lean!

10:01.620 --> 10:03.250
<i>Oh no!</i>

10:07.130 --> 10:09.340
<i>Dr. Toto'll get mad at me!</i>

10:10.710 --> 10:11.800
<i>Lean!</i>

10:13.590 --> 10:16.300
<i>Good kitty, Lean. Hold still.</i>

10:17.680 --> 10:19.180
<i>Lean!</i>

10:20.980 --> 10:23.390
Lean, where are you?

10:23.390 --> 10:25.270
It's not scary anymore.

10:25.270 --> 10:26.690
Come on out.

10:30.480 --> 10:31.530
Lean?

10:42.330 --> 10:46.130
This is naught compared to the icy prison of Cocytus.

10:46.630 --> 10:48.210
There's a tiny thingy inside.

10:48.210 --> 10:49.710
I am <i>not</i> tiny!

10:50.670 --> 10:54.590
Mine name is BUER, philosopher of hell.

10:55.010 --> 10:56.590
Philosopher?

10:56.590 --> 10:57.510
Indeed.

10:57.510 --> 10:58.930
What a weird petroid.

10:58.930 --> 11:00.640
I wonder if someone left it behind.

11:00.640 --> 11:02.220
I am no one's possession!

11:03.020 --> 11:07.730
I thank thee for liberating me, little lady.

11:09.230 --> 11:10.610
Don't mention it.

11:14.900 --> 11:18.120
I don't have time to play around with this tiny thingy!

11:18.620 --> 11:20.530
I need to find Lean!

11:20.530 --> 11:23.500
BUER is the name I would have thee call me, little lady.

11:23.870 --> 11:26.120
Now then, who is this Lean?

11:29.670 --> 11:33.090
Lean is a kitten who followed me in here.

11:33.090 --> 11:33.920
I see.

11:33.920 --> 11:36.300
But pets aren't allowed in the hospital.

11:36.300 --> 11:41.680
It'll be bad if somebody finds him,
so I need to find him first.

11:41.680 --> 11:43.770
Aye, I understand thy situation.

11:43.770 --> 11:46.520
In that case, thou canst rely upon mine assistance.

11:46.520 --> 11:48.940
Thank you! But...

11:49.480 --> 11:50.810
What is the matter?

11:53.190 --> 11:56.150
If Dr. Toto finds out I brought Lean,

11:56.150 --> 11:58.860
he'll get mad at me.

11:58.860 --> 12:01.580
Thou needest not be troubled, little lady.

12:01.580 --> 12:04.500
Thou shalt have all that thou holdest dear.

12:04.870 --> 12:09.630
Little girls are the only beings
who get to wish for everything.

12:10.580 --> 12:11.460
Okay.

12:13.090 --> 12:14.300
Thank you.

12:14.300 --> 12:18.430
No gratitude necessary. I did but speak the truth.

12:18.430 --> 12:24.220
Now let us go, on the dazzling
journey of love we call a search!

12:44.240 --> 12:46.330
I want a progress report.

12:47.160 --> 12:51.290
We've penetrated the outermost layer of the logic barrier, as well as layers two and three.

12:51.290 --> 12:54.090
Access to layer four is still underway.

12:54.090 --> 12:57.670
Support AI array one.
Core temperature up twenty points.

12:57.670 --> 13:00.720
Array two connected, array three on standby.

13:00.720 --> 13:05.100
Colonel, a large-scale network outage is occurring on the surface.

13:05.100 --> 13:07.930
Not a problem. Continue the work.

13:09.310 --> 13:10.310
BUER...

13:12.940 --> 13:15.110
You're going to oppose me to the very end?

13:16.280 --> 13:20.450
Does this Lean not have a tracking marker on it?

13:20.450 --> 13:22.530
Those ones for pets?

13:22.530 --> 13:26.200
You know, his collar might have one.

13:26.200 --> 13:28.540
Then dost thou know the ID?

13:29.460 --> 13:30.710
It's here.

13:36.590 --> 13:37.590
Well?

13:39.670 --> 13:42.180
There has been a network outage.

13:43.180 --> 13:46.600
A great darkness is blinding mine eyes.

13:46.600 --> 13:48.060
What do you mean?

13:49.430 --> 13:51.350
I cannot find it.

13:52.270 --> 13:55.360
Problem. BUER is gone.

13:55.770 --> 13:57.360
Maybe he got lost?

13:57.360 --> 13:58.690
He fled.

13:59.820 --> 14:03.030
He's still nearby. There are no threats on the premises.

14:03.030 --> 14:04.870
Do you know where he is?

14:05.740 --> 14:06.740
This way.

14:09.790 --> 14:12.410
Dr. Toto's gonna hate me...

14:12.410 --> 14:15.000
Lean, where'd you go?

14:15.000 --> 14:16.630
What do I do!?

14:17.840 --> 14:22.800
While this mine heart flutter, tears suit not the little lady.

14:22.800 --> 14:24.430
Entrust it to me.

14:24.430 --> 14:26.890
But you're no help!

14:33.690 --> 14:35.730
It seems the time hath come

14:35.730 --> 14:38.730
for the philosopher of hell... to get serious.

14:43.650 --> 14:47.830
None can evade the gaze of the philosopher of hell!

14:47.830 --> 14:49.160
Never mind the tracker!

14:49.160 --> 14:53.960
Should it approach, my fifth hoof shall vibrate!

14:54.500 --> 14:56.250
Small animal spotted!

15:01.130 --> 15:03.470
You really found him! Lean!

15:04.470 --> 15:05.880
Lean, wait!

15:06.470 --> 15:08.140
Come on, Lean!

15:11.350 --> 15:12.350
Lean!

15:17.770 --> 15:19.150
Oh, my.

15:19.520 --> 15:21.730
A kitty, in a place like this?

15:27.530 --> 15:29.910
I lost track of Lean again.

15:29.910 --> 15:32.160
Grievest not, little lady.

15:32.160 --> 15:35.500
What distress can there be, with me by thy side?

15:36.960 --> 15:38.880
Thanks, tiny thingy.

15:38.880 --> 15:43.170
Once we find Lean, we'll also go find your owner.

15:49.510 --> 15:53.520
I would not be averse to napping by thy side a while longer.

15:54.680 --> 15:56.230
You don't want to go home?

15:57.140 --> 15:58.770
Do you get bullied!?

15:58.770 --> 16:00.730
Nay, I am not bullied!

16:03.070 --> 16:06.110
Nothing can bind me, the demon king,

16:06.110 --> 16:08.610
but 'tis nice to visit the human world occasionally.

16:10.200 --> 16:13.240
Hast thou come here for treatment, little lady?

16:13.240 --> 16:14.160
Yeah.

16:14.660 --> 16:16.620
This leg's temporary.

16:16.620 --> 16:19.080
I'm getting it switched with a new one today.

16:21.210 --> 16:23.880
The new one will be really nice!

16:23.880 --> 16:27.550
Grandma was saying it's sure to go well with this outfit!

16:29.800 --> 16:34.770
<i>Robed in a white dress, she alights my heart!</i>

16:35.390 --> 16:37.430
<i>No lecher could resist!</i>

16:37.850 --> 16:41.360
It brings out thy life's glow.

16:41.360 --> 16:43.570
Oh, there's BUER.

16:44.070 --> 16:45.690
Ah, maiden!

16:45.690 --> 16:47.950
This reunion is an inevitability of...

16:51.570 --> 16:52.780
fate...

16:54.580 --> 16:57.830
Is she your owner?

16:59.960 --> 17:01.330
So cute!

17:01.330 --> 17:04.960
Admire me as well, maiden!

17:04.960 --> 17:08.590
Oh, my, it's Nene and Clarion.

17:09.470 --> 17:10.680
Lean!

17:10.680 --> 17:13.350
Oh, do you know this kitty?

17:17.350 --> 17:20.690
So I was going for a stroll, when I came across Lean.

17:20.690 --> 17:22.480
So that's what happened.

17:23.190 --> 17:26.730
You know how we keep having network outages these days?

17:27.230 --> 17:30.450
I've been hospitalized, in case
something were to happen again.

17:31.280 --> 17:36.370
Miss Amy Gilliam. Miss Amy Gilliam.
Please come to examination room three.

17:37.870 --> 17:39.330
Time for your check-up.

17:39.330 --> 17:40.290
I'm going.

17:40.290 --> 17:42.960
We'll watch the cat for you.

17:42.960 --> 17:43.750
Thanks!

17:44.250 --> 17:47.340
Amy, don't run inside the...

17:47.880 --> 17:48.760
hospital...

17:49.550 --> 17:51.300
Amy...

17:53.590 --> 17:56.890
I can't go see Dr. Toto like this!

17:57.310 --> 18:00.140
F-For now, let's borrow a hospital robe.

18:00.140 --> 18:03.400
No! It has to be my dress!

18:05.480 --> 18:10.900
I have a sewing set... but I doubt that can be fixed quickly.

18:10.900 --> 18:12.700
Indeed it can.

18:13.910 --> 18:15.870
Oh! Right!

18:16.240 --> 18:18.830
Amy, wait right there.

18:18.830 --> 18:19.790
Okay...

18:19.790 --> 18:21.620
Be sure not to peek.

18:28.630 --> 18:31.260
Pandora Device, open!

18:33.510 --> 18:36.680
Decode skill, Elpis Series.

18:42.140 --> 18:43.640
Couturier!

18:57.700 --> 18:59.080
Would you like some candy?

18:59.080 --> 19:00.120
Sure.

19:00.740 --> 19:02.160
Here you go!

19:09.420 --> 19:12.920
Wow! Wow, wow, wow!

19:16.680 --> 19:19.010
Thank you, Miss Nene!

19:23.020 --> 19:24.520
Miss Nene!

19:33.780 --> 19:36.990
Oh, so you live at that camp in the park.

19:36.990 --> 19:37.780
Yeah!

19:40.780 --> 19:43.540
Thanks for walking me back, Nene.

19:43.540 --> 19:44.540
No problem.

19:44.540 --> 19:45.620
And Clarin.

19:45.620 --> 19:46.710
Clarion.

19:46.710 --> 19:48.920
Hast thou forgotten someone?

19:49.880 --> 19:51.630
Thank you too, tiny thingy.

19:51.630 --> 19:54.800
That's the philosopher of hell, BUER!

20:20.820 --> 20:22.280
Why?

20:22.280 --> 20:23.620
Grandma...

20:27.210 --> 20:28.620
Everyone...

20:31.670 --> 20:35.800
They're all gone! Where'd they go!?

20:35.800 --> 20:37.220
Amy...

20:40.970 --> 20:42.430
Grandma!?

20:42.430 --> 20:45.930
Grandma! It's Amy!

20:46.350 --> 20:47.730
Where are you?

20:47.730 --> 20:52.310
Uh-huh. Uh-huh. Uh-huh, okay.

20:52.900 --> 20:55.320
That's fine, I'll be right there.

20:55.320 --> 20:56.400
Your grandma?

20:56.400 --> 20:57.440
Yeah.

20:57.440 --> 21:02.320
She said some CDF guys came,
and they made everybody evacuate.

21:02.320 --> 21:03.280
Where to?

21:03.870 --> 21:05.160
Um...

21:05.580 --> 21:08.210
I know where that is! I'll take you there.

21:08.210 --> 21:09.660
Really!?

21:25.640 --> 21:27.180
Clarin, let's go.

21:29.850 --> 21:32.980
I know this outfit is going to surprise Grandma!

21:32.980 --> 21:35.440
I hope it does.

21:56.590 --> 21:58.590
Clarin, let's go!

21:58.590 --> 22:00.260
Let's go!

22:04.680 --> 22:06.760
Come on, Clarin.

22:06.760 --> 22:08.390
The lesbians show their colors!

22:08.390 --> 22:11.350
A lesbo tower hath been erected on a tropical isl—

22:41.050 --> 22:44.050
Accessing the device named nature

22:44.050 --> 22:47.050
The circuit of infinite synapses

22:47.050 --> 22:47.600
read

22:47.600 --> 22:48.140
write

22:48.140 --> 22:48.810
enter

22:48.810 --> 22:49.430
code

22:49.430 --> 22:52.810
Sharing tools can lead to unavoidable situations

22:52.930 --> 22:54.890
Lesbians? What was BUER so excited about?

22:53.520 --> 23:04.110
{talk}{this is pandoradio, it'll change each week, ignore this segemnt}

22:54.890 --> 22:56.440
It's not important.

22:56.440 --> 22:59.020
I wonder if that tower really exists.
I'd love to go!

22:59.020 --> 23:01.320
You and I could look at the night sky together, as we...

23:01.320 --> 23:04.030
I see you have at least a rough
understanding of the matter.

23:04.110 --> 23:05.490
Saving data

23:05.490 --> 23:06.870
Strengthening predictions

23:06.870 --> 23:09.870
Even my latest updates

23:09.870 --> 23:15.170
can't help explain why you're so nice to me

23:15.170 --> 23:16.750
Error error

23:16.750 --> 23:18.250
parameter

23:18.250 --> 23:21.630
Please help me understand

23:21.630 --> 23:23.800
where these emotions came from.

23:23.800 --> 23:26.970
Find me at the end of this labrynth

23:26.970 --> 23:29.720
of feelings I can no longer control

23:29.720 --> 23:31.720
I understand the concept of emotions

23:31.720 --> 23:35.100
but I can't make any sense of my own

23:35.480 --> 23:38.100
I want to pull out these cords

23:38.440 --> 23:40.860
and head straight to you

23:40.860 --> 23:43.280
I won't come to understand love

23:43.280 --> 23:47.030
without having you here with me

23:52.990 --> 23:55.830
l am BUER, the demon king, philosopher of hell.

23:55.830 --> 23:56.960
Why are you a lion?

23:56.960 --> 23:59.170
Precisely: the head of the lion, and five legs of the goat.

23:59.170 --> 24:00.840
The ancient grimoire <i>Lemegeton</i> states that—

24:00.840 --> 24:03.170
You know, that tiny front leg of yours is cute!

24:03.170 --> 24:04.840
It is <i>not</i> tiny!
